## Course overview

Computer Science develops computational thinking and practical programming skill. Students learn how computers and networks work, how to design and build software, and how computing shapes society.

## What you will study

- **Computational thinking and problem-solving**: algorithms and program design.
- **Programming**: fundamentals through to object-oriented design.
- **Computer organisation and architecture**.
- **Networks and the internet**.
- **Databases and abstract data structures** (extended at HL).

## Assessment

| Component | HL | SL | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Paper 1 | 40% | 45% | Concepts and problem-solving |
| Paper 2 | 20% | 25% | Option topic (e.g. databases, web science) |
| Paper 3 (HL) | 20% | - | Case study analysis |
| Internal Assessment | 20% | 30% | A developed software solution to a real problem |
